<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gardizi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Abu Sa'id Gardizi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gardizi was a Persian historian of the 11th century, from Gardez in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, who wrote the Zayn al-Akhbar around 1050 for the Ghaznavid sultan Abd al-Rashid. The work is a history of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a> and Khurasan, and its chapter on the Turks and their neighbours is a key source for the steppe peoples, including the Kimek, Kyrgyz and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a>.</p></div>
